  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">For developers, exchanges, and wallet creators, the <strong id=\"\">JSON-RPC Radix Node API</strong> offers a simple way of interacting with the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Public Network</strong></a> by connecting to an <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-full-node-validator-node-and-archive-node\"><strong id=\"\">archive node</strong></a> that offers the API endpoint. <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radix\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong></a> provides archive nodes for public use; however, often it is preferable for the client user to maintain one of their own. Please visit <a id=\"\" href=\"https://docs.radixdlt.com/main/index.html\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Tech Docs</strong></a> for more information about using the JSON-RPC Radix Node API and setting up an archive node.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://docs.radixdlt.com/main/index.html\"><strong id=\"\">Welcome to the Radix Tech Docs</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radix-node-software\"><strong id=\"\">What is Radix Node software?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-full-node-validator-node-and-archive-node\"><strong id=\"\">What's the difference between a full node, validator node, and archive node?</strong></a></li></ul>",
